# Swift / iOS

Follow [The Swift Programming Language](https://www.swift.org/documentation/) and [API Design Guidelines](https://www.swift.org/documentation/). Names: `ScanStore`, `SavedScan`, `ScanSessionView`.

- Deployment: iOS 17+. Link **system** `RoomPlan` + `ARKit` + `RealityKit` via Xcode; **no CocoaPods**, no root `Package.swift` for MVP
- Scan UI: `RoomCaptureView` + `RoomCaptureViewDelegate` (not `RoomCaptureSessionDelegate` unless leaving the stock view)
- Persist `CapturedRoom` Codable; export USDZ via `CapturedRoom.export`
- In-app preview: RealityKit `ARView` in `.nonAR` walkthrough (`RoomPreviewView` / `RoomWalkthroughARView`)
- Do not wrap `QLPreviewController` for in-app preview
- Share still sends USDZ; receivers may open it in system Quick Look
- Do not invent coaching copy — `RoomCaptureView` already instructs the user
- Exhaustive `switch` on RoomPlan enums (`Confidence`, categories): `default` must assign `never`

```swift
// ❌ BAD
func captureSession(_ session: RoomCaptureSession, didEndWith data: CapturedRoomData) {}

// ✅ GOOD
func captureView(shouldPresent roomData: CapturedRoomData, error: Error?) -> Bool { true }
func captureView(didPresent processedResult: CapturedRoom, error: Error?) { onComplete(...) }
// Coordinator: encode(with:) + init?(coder:) stubs required by RoomCaptureViewDelegate
```
